# Default User Roles

Seeded on install; see `permissions.mdc` for semantics. Canonical catalogs:
`backend/src/config/roles.js` (identity, aliases, hierarchy) and `BASE_ROLE_PERMISSIONS` /
`ROLE_PERMISSION_TEMPLATES` in `backend/src/config/permissions.js` (packs).
`ROLE_PERMISSIONS` is the resolved export both are folded into. Counts below are asserted
by `backend/src/tests/config/permissions.test.js`.

## Structure

- **70 canonical roles**, all uppercase snake_case (`LAB_TECH`, `HOUSE_KEEPER`). Always
  write the canonical code; the lowercase job-title forms below are display names, not
  identifiers.
- **40 base packs** in `BASE_ROLE_PERMISSIONS`. The other **30 roles** are
  `ROLE_PERMISSION_TEMPLATES` entries that reuse a parent's pack byte-for-byte
  (`MIDWIFE` → `NURSE`, `DENTIST` → `DOCTOR`). A template role exists for job title and
  ABAC scope, not for different rights.
- The 40 base packs produce **38 distinct permission sets**. Two pairs are byte-identical
  and stay separate roles for job title and ABAC scope: `AMBULANCE_OPERATOR` ≡ `EMT`, and
  `SURGEON` ≡ `ANESTHESIOLOGIST`. That set is pinned by test — any *new* duplicate is a
  bug: give the role rights of its own, or make it a `ROLE_PERMISSION_TEMPLATES` entry.
- **40 `LEGACY_ROLE_ALIASES`** map historical names onto canonical codes
  (`SUPER_ADMIN` → `PLATFORM_ADMIN`, `RADIOGRAPHER` → `RADIOLOGY_TECH`,
  `AMBULANCE_DRIVER` → `AMBULANCE_OPERATOR`). `normalizeRoleName` resolves them. No alias
  key may itself be a canonical role code — `EMT`, `PARAMEDIC` and `CHARGE_NURSE` stay
  distinct roles, not aliases.
- A user may hold several roles via `user_role`; rights are the **union** of their packs.
- `reports:read` is in every shipped pack, and is re-granted as a baseline after plan
  gating regardless (`permissions.mdc`, step 5).

## Client-side role resolution

`AppRole` (`frontend/lib/core/permissions/access_policy.dart`) carries only the **27
shell-focus roles**. Every canonical role still resolves to a client pack for JWT-only
restore, through one of three paths, checked in this order:

1. `_exactRolePermissionPacks` — roles whose backend pack matches no `AppRole` pack
   (`ACCOUNTANT`, `OPD_DOCTOR`, `ICU_DOCTOR`, `PHARMACY_BILLING`, `SURGEON`,
   `ANESTHESIOLOGIST`, `EMERGENCY_PHYSICIAN`, `CHARGE_NURSE`, `PATHOLOGIST`,
   `PHARMACY_TECHNICIAN`, `MEDICAL_CODER`, `PARAMEDIC`).
2. `_normalizeRole` — canonical `AppRole` codes plus display/legacy aliases.
3. `_extendedRolePermissionParents` — template roles that mirror a parent pack exactly.

A role code must appear in at most one of paths 1 and 3. Roles outside `AppRole` produce no
`AppRole`, so `hasRole` is false for them and the shell applies permission-domain scoping,
while their rights still apply. Live rights always come from `/auth/me`; role packs are the
pre-hydration fallback only, and are never unioned on top of backend grants.
`frontend/test/core/permissions/role_pack_parity_test.dart` asserts every canonical role
resolves.

## Shipped roles and their top-level destinations

Destinations are the workspaces the pack's entry keys open, **before** plan gating. Every
staff role also has `profile:read` and `reports:read`.

| Role | Destinations |
| ---- | ------------ |
| `PLATFORM_OWNER` | everything, all tenants |
| `PLATFORM_ADMIN` | everything except `platform:owner` |
| `TENANT_ADMIN` | every workspace except `/subscriptions`, incl. Setup and Access admin; tenant scope |
| `FACILITY_ADMIN` | same set, facility scope (no `tenant:admin`) |
| `INTEGRATION_ADMIN` | Integrations, Reports (`integration` is version-disabled) |
| `DOCTOR` | Patients, OPD, IPD, ICU, Clinical, Theatre, Reports |
| `OPD_DOCTOR` | Patients, OPD, Clinical, Reports |
| `ICU_DOCTOR` | Patients, IPD, ICU, Clinical, Reports |
| `SURGEON` / `ANESTHESIOLOGIST` | Patients, IPD, ICU, Clinical, Theatre, Reports (no OPD) |
| `EMERGENCY_PHYSICIAN` | Patients, OPD, IPD, ICU, Clinical, Reports (no Theatre) |
| `NURSE` | Patients, OPD, IPD, ICU, Nursing, Clinical, Discharge, Lab, Reports |
| `CHARGE_NURSE` | `NURSE` plus `unit:read`, `roster:read`, `roster:write` |
| `RECEPTIONIST` | Reception, Patients, Reports |
| `LAB_TECH` | Patients, Lab, Reports |
| `PATHOLOGIST` | `LAB_TECH` plus `clinical:read` |
| `RADIOLOGY_TECH` | Patients, Radiology, Reports |
| `PHARMACIST` | Pharmacy, Reports (+ `pricing:pharmacy_*`, `patient:read`) |
| `PHARMACY_TECHNICIAN` | Pharmacy read-only (no `pharmacy:write`, no pricing) |
| `PHARMACY_BILLING` | Pharmacy cashier: `billing:*`, `pricing:pharmacy_*`, `pharmacy:read`, `claims:read`, `last_office:*`, `patient:read` |
| `BILLING` | Billing, Claims, Reports (+ `pricing:facility_*`, `last_office:*`, `financial:approve`) |
| `MEDICAL_CODER` | Patients, Billing (read), Claims, Reports — no billing write or approve |
| `ACCOUNTANT` | Billing, Accounts, Claims, Reports (+ `financial:approve`; no `last_office:*`) |
| `HR` / `HR_STAFF` | HR, Reports, Setup (facility users/roles/permissions tabs) |
| `UNIT_MANAGER`, `WARD_MANAGER`, `ICU_MANAGER`, `THEATRE_MANAGER` | unit-scoped management packs |
| `OPERATIONS`, `HOUSE_KEEPER`, `BIOMED`, `MORTUARY_STAFF`, `MORTUARY_MANAGER`, `HOUSEKEEPING_MANAGER`, `BIOMED_MANAGER` | version-disabled domains — no reachable destination this release |
| `AMBULANCE_OPERATOR`, `PARAMEDIC`, `EMT` | emergency packs; `emergency` is version-disabled |
| `PATIENT` | own patient data only |
| `OTHER` / `VISITOR_GUEST` | limited visitor info only |

Corrections against earlier drafts of this file, verified against `BASE_ROLE_PERMISSIONS`:

- `DOCTOR` does **not** hold `nursing:read`. Nursing is a nurse/ward destination; doctors
  reach nursing context through Clinical.
- `RECEPTIONIST` does **not** hold `billing:read` or `evidence:export`. There is no
  receptionist billing view.
- `PHARMACIST` does **not** hold `billing:read` or `patients:read`. Patient details are
  reachable only via pharmacy/dashboard embeds; the cashier pack is `PHARMACY_BILLING`.
- No admin role reaches `/subscriptions`. That route requires `platform:owner` or
  `platform:admin` *and* the matching role; tenant admins use the shell's upgrade/renew
  chrome, gated by `subscriptions:*`.
- There is no `triage` permission domain or module. Triage is part of the
  `scheduling-queue` module and the nursing packs.

## Accounts role matrix

- **Have Accounts rights:** `ACCOUNTANT`, `PLATFORM_OWNER`, `PLATFORM_ADMIN`,
  `TENANT_ADMIN`, `FACILITY_ADMIN` (the last two via admin access packs).
- **Do not have Accounts rights by default:** `HR` / `HR_STAFF`, billing-only packs, and
  every non-admin clinical/ops pack, unless Access admin assigns `accounts:*` on a custom
  role. Payroll may later post summary journals into Accounts without opening `/accounts`.
- Module `facility-accounts` (BASIC) is a second gate; role keys alone do not open
  `/accounts` when the module is not entitled.
- Approve / Reject additionally needs `financial:approve`, which maps to `billing-payments`
  and is capped at ADVANCED — so it needs an Advanced package **and** both
  `facility-accounts` and `billing-payments` entitled, even though the desk opens at Basic.
- See `.cursor/finance/_shared/permissions-and-entitlements.md`.

## Administration

- Admins may add custom roles using the same vocabulary; custom roles are evaluated by
  permission pack, not by name (`custom-role-rbac.test.js`).
- Reset must restore this matrix atomically and stay auditable.
- Failed changes must roll back completely.
- UI and API must deny unauthorized menus, actions, and workflows.

